QuestGuidance.Register("en",10,{
[289]="70015AD6\n1\tBring an infused garnet to Perimbant\tPerimbant has asked you to bring him an infused garnet to act as the heart of the spell that is to be woven into your weapon. Where such a gem may be obtained, he does not know.\n2\tTalk to Perimbant to travel to Pembar\tPerimbant can be found in Echad Dúnann, just west of the gates of Moria. Perimbant has bidden you to speak with him when you are ready to travel to the ruins of Pembar to liberate it from the flight of drakes.\n3\tBring the empowered garnet to Perimbant\tPerimbant can be found in Echad Dúnann, west of the gates of Moria. You should return to Perimbant to complete the enhancement of your weapon.\n",
[290]="7006EC1C\n1\tMaghôrdo has asked you to scare off the seagulls loitering around the harbour.\t\n2\tTalk to Maghôrdo\tYou have scared off many seagulls loitering around the harbour, as Maghôrdo asked. You should report to Maghôrdo at Furtherholm's harbour, near the waterfall.\n",
[291]="70019D36\n1\tLeave the flower for Nimrodel at her statue\tA statue of Nimrodel can be found north of Pennasdir along the path, beyond the ladders to Telain Galadhrim. Pennasdir has asked you to place a flower on the silver plate at the feet of a statue of Nimrodel.\n2\tTalk to Pennasdir upon Telain Glorelloth\tPennasdir is on Telain Glorelloth, in Caras Galadhon. You have left the flower for Nimrodel by her statue and should return now to Pennasdir.\n",
[292]="700607AC\n1\tTalk to Gandalf the Grey\tTalk to Gandalf the Grey.\n2\tPick up fireworks crates (total: 2)\tPick up fireworks crates from the cart.\n3\tSet up the fireworks display at the first launch location\030Thwart nosey hobbits\tSet up the fireworks display at the first launch location. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tPick up more fireworks crates (total: 2)\tPick up more fireworks crates from the cart.\n5\tSet up the fireworks display at the second launch location\tSet up the fireworks display at the second launch location. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n6\tPick up even more fireworks crates (total: 2)\tPick up even more fireworks crates from the cart.\n7\tSet up the fireworks display at the final launch location\tSet up the fireworks display at the final launch location. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n8\tTalk to Gandalf the Grey to launch the fireworks display\tTalk to Gandalf the Grey to launch the fireworks display.\n",
[293]="700607E6\n1\tComplete 'A Flurry of Fireworks'\tComplete 'A Flurry of Fireworks'.\n",
[294]="7004A8D5\n1\tDisguise yourself as the Silent One and enter Cirith Ungol\tCirith Ungol can be found high above you on a mountainside of the Ephel Dúath to the north of Dath Nethryn. Legolas has asked you to disguise yourself as the Silent One and sneak into Cirith Ungol to learn more of the Orcs' plans and how they came to bargain with Shelob.\n2\tPass through the shattered gate of Cirith Ungol\tThe shattered gate of Cirith Ungol faces eastward from the entrance. You have entered Cirith Ungol and should now pass through the gate.\n3\tFind Captain Róglarg in the courtyard of Cirith Ungol\tCaptain Róglarg can be found in the courtyard of Cirith Ungol. You have disguised yourself as the Silent One and snuck into Cirith Ungol. You should now find Captain Róglarg.\n",
[295]="700577C3\n1\tComplete 'In Celebration of Midsummer' three more times\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three more days!\n2\tComplete 'In Celebration of Midsummer' (total: 3)\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three more days!\n3\tTalk to Faeleth in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\030Talk to Captain Khâtaphos at Furtherholm in the Shield Isles\tFaeleth can be found in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Faeleth would like to thank you for your continued celebration of Midsummer.\n",
[296]="700577C1\n1\tComplete 'In Celebration of Midsummer' three more times\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three more days!\n2\tComplete 'In Celebration of Midsummer' (total: 3)\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three more days!\n3\tTalk to Faeleth in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\030Talk to Captain Khâtaphos at Furtherholm in the Shield Isles\tFaeleth can be found in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Faeleth would like to thank you for your continued celebration of Midsummer.\n",
[297]="700577C2\n1\tComplete 'In Celebration of Midsummer' three more times\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three more days!\n2\tComplete 'In Celebration of Midsummer' (total: 3)\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three more days!\n3\tTalk to Faeleth in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\030Talk to Captain Khâtaphos at Furtherholm in the Shield Isles\tFaeleth can be found in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Faeleth would like to thank you for your continued celebration of Midsummer.\n",
[298]="700577C5\n1\tComplete 'In Celebration of Midsummer' three times\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for three days!\n2\tComplete 'In Celebration of Midsummer' (total: 3)\tAs Midsummer's Day approaches, the peoples of Middle-earth come together to celebrate the great festival of Midsummer. Revel in the celebration of dance, merriment, and love with your family and fellows for five days!\n3\tTalk to Faeleth in Minas Tirith (Midsummer)\030Talk to Captain Khâtaphos at Furtherholm in the Shield Isles\tFaeleth can be found in Minas Tirith (Midsummer). Faeleth would like to thank you for your continued celebration of Midsummer.\n",
[299]="70019008\n1\tEnter the hedge-maze\tThe entrance to the hedge-maze is near the festival grounds in the Horse-fields, a distance to the north of Bree-town. Gil Plover has challenged you to get through the maze, from start to finish, before the time runs out. The time he has allotted is the same amount of time of his record run.\n2\tFind your way out before the time expires\tThe exit to the hedge-maze is around here somewhere...or is it? You should try to find your way out of the maze before the time runs out. Gil Plover got out in just over one minute; can you navigate the paths in less? This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Gil Plover outside the maze in the Horse-fields\tGil Plover is standing near the hedge maze, which is very near the festival grounds of Bree-land, north of Bree-town. You should speak with Gil Plover, for you can show him that you are the fastest maze-runner of all.\n",
[300]="70015E0A\n1\tSearch for some sign of Thorlák\tThorlák headed into the Redhorn Gate, north-east of Echad Dúnann. Hjór has asked that you search the Redhorn Gate for signs of Thorlák.\n2\tTalk to Hjór\tHjór is at Echad Dúnann, south-west of the Redhorn Gate. You should return to Hjór and tell him what you found in the Redhorn Gate.\n",
[301]="7004A380\n1\tVisit the Foothold in Udûn\tYou should visit the Foothold in Udûn and remind them of their duty to send regular reports up to High Captain Sador.\n2\tTalk to Mulnír\030Talk to Barathron\tYou should find someone to talk to in the Foothold in Udûn and remind them of their duty to send regular reports up to High Captain Sador.\n",
[302]="7003E433\n1\tExplore and protect Fangorn Forest with Quickbeam's Huorn\tQuickbeam wishes for you to investigate various areas throughout Fangorn Forest. Quickbeam has asked that you explore Fangorn Forest and quell any problems you and his Huorn observe.\n2\tTalk to Quickbeam's Huorn\tQuickbeam's Huorn can be found at your side or can be called using your whistle. You have explored every part of the forest with Quickbeam's Huorn. You should release the Huorn back into the trees and speak to Quickbeam.\n3\tTalk to Quickbeam\tQuickbeam can be found at Derndingle in south-eastern Fangorn Forest. You have released your Huorn companion and should now speak to Quickbeam of what you have done.\n",
[303]="700413CE\n1\tDefeat spiders in Ringló Vale (total: 8)\030Destroy spider webs (total: 12)\030Investigate the source of the spider infestation\tSpiders infest the woods in the western part of Ringló Vale. Stem the spider infestation in Ringló Vale.\n2\tDefeat the Weft-mother\tThe Weft-mother can be found inside the spider infested cave. You should defeat the Weft-mother.\n3\tSpeak with Authest\tThe beacon of Eilendoth is located south-west of Ethring in Ringló Vale. You should speak with Authest.\n4\tSpeak with Borhador\tBorhador can be found in The Crossing-hall. You should speak with Borhador.\n",
[304]="7004DDF5\n1\tTravel to the entrance of Lake-town and speak to the guards\tOne of the guards at the entrance to Lake-town might be able to tell you more about the last days of Esgaroth, before the dragon Smaug was defeated. On this anniversary of Bilbo's arrival at Esgaroth, what do the residents of the town remember of the Burglar?\n2\tTalk to Várthrek at the entrance to Lake-town\tOne of the guards at the entrance to Lake-town might be able to tell you more about the last days of Esgaroth, before the dragon Smaug was defeated. On this anniversary of Bilbo's arrival at Esgaroth, what do the residents of the town remember of the Burglar?\n3\tFind the oldest resident of Lake-town and ask him about the death of Smaug\tLóskarl is the oldest resident of Lake-town, and he might be able to tell you what he remembers of the death of Smaug. Várthrek told you that Lóskarl often holds court in the Dragonbone Inn.\n4\tTravel to Loeglond, the city of the Raft-elves\tLóskarl told you there were Raft-elves present when Bilbo and the dwarves came to Lake-town, and if they are still alive they might be able to tell you more than he can. You should visit Loeglond and see if you can find these Raft-elves.\n5\tYou learned that a number of Raft-elves were present at Esgaroth when the dwarves and Bilbo arrived to reclaim the Lonely Mountain. If you can find some of these Elves in Loeglond, they might tell you more about their experience.\t\n6\tFind Celethros somewhere near the dungeons of Felegoth, in Eryn Lasgalen\tCelethros is somewhere near the dungeons of Felegoth, in Eryn Lasgalen.\n7\tTalk to Bilbo in the Hall of Fire, in Rivendell\tBilbo Baggins is in the Hall of Fire, in Rivendell.\n",
[305]="70009A59\n1\tRetrieve the formal complaint from Ronald Dwale\tRonald Dwale is at Hob Hillbrow's home at the Bullroarer's Sward in Dwaling. Hob Hillbrow has asked you to retrieve the formal complaint he asked Ronald Dwale to draft.\n2\tUse Doorbell\tWill Tuffin is in the big hole in Dwaling centre. Deliver the formal complaint to Will Tuffin.\n3\tTalk to Hob Hillbrow\tHob Hillbrow is at his home at the Bullroarer's Sward in Dwaling. You should return to Hob Hillbrow and tell him of Will Tuffin's response.\n4\tTalk to Bob Greeneaves\tBob Greeneaves is at Hob Hillbrow's home at the Bullroarer's Sward in Dwaling. Talk to Bob Greeneaves to gain access to the big hole to deliver the letter.\n5\tReturn to Hob Hillbrow\tHob Hillbrow is at his home at the Bullroarer's Sward in Dwaling, south of town centre. You should return to Hob Hillbrow with word of your success and his letter.\n",
[306]="7006BF73\n1\tDefeat Orcs in the Fotak-dâr camp within Kûr Anzar (total: 9)\030Defeat Shalblúg in Fotak-dâr\tDefeat the Orcs encamped in Fotak-dâr near the top of Kûr Anzar, including their leader, Shalblúg. Kûr Anzar is located east of Urmâkh.\n2\tReturn to Numûru in Urmâkh\tReturn to Numûru in Urmâkh with news of your triumph.\n",
[307]="7004C993\n1\tComplete 'A Festive Flurry (Intro)'\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities to receive gifts!\n2\tComplete 'A Festive Flurry (Intermediate)'\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three more days!\n3\tComplete 'A Festive Flurry (Advanced)'\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three more days!\n4\tComplete 'A Festive Flurry (Final)'\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities for three more days!\n5\tTalk to Mara Sandydowns\tCompleted.\n",
[308]="7005177E\n1\tComplete 'A Bountiful Harvest (Intro)'\tEvery day there is something to do in the Harvest Festival, both at the Party Tree, in Wistmead, and for Treats and Trickery. Join in the autumnal activities to receive gifts!\n2\tComplete 'A Bountiful Harvest (Intermediate)'\tEvery day there is something to do in the Harvest Festival, both at the Party Tree, in Wistmead, and for Treats and Trickery. Join in the autumnal activities for five more days!\n3\tComplete 'A Bountiful Harvest (Advanced)'\tEvery day there is something to do in the Harvest Festival, both at the Party Tree, in Wistmead, and for Treats and Trickery. Join in the autumnal activities for five more days!\n4\tComplete 'A Bountiful Harvest (Final)'\tEvery day there is something to do in the Harvest Festival, both at the Party Tree, in Wistmead, and for Treats and Trickery. Join in the autumnal activities for five more days!\n5\tYou should return to Rosa Hornblower, who can be found near the Party Tree and in Wistmead.\t\n",
[309]="70048C94\n1\tDestroy Uruk brew (total: 10)\tUruk brew barrels can be found in Kala-gijak. You should destroy Uruk brew barrels.\n2\tTalk to Faeron\tFaeron can be found outside Kala-gijak. You should talk to Faeron.\n",
[310]="70071CD1\n1\tDefeat goblin raiders in Glúkroz (total: 7)\030Defeat goblin watch-keeps in Glúkroz (total: 5)\030Defeat goblin sappers in Glúkroz (total: 3)\tDefeat goblins at Glúkroz to send a message that the goblin raiders there should stay far from Sen Chatâk. Glúkroz can be found north-east of Sen Chatâk.\n2\tReturn to Elder Jangâli in Sen Chatâk\tReturn to Elder Jangâli in Sen Chatâk with news of your victory.\n",
[311]="70015E1F\n1\tDefeat fell holly-tenders (total: 8)\030Defeat Huorns (total: 8)\tHuorns, the great trees that move about freely, and holly-tenders can be found throughout Glâd Ereg. Lithuilas has asked you to defeat the Huorns and holly-tenders which have been stirred to wrath. He recommends you take friends with you.\n2\tTalk to Lithuilas at Gwingris\tLithuilas is at Gwingris, north of Glâd Ereg. Lithuilas will want to know of your success.\n",
[312]="7006C6ED\n1\tSpeak with Raphûz about his concerns\tRaphûz requested your advice. You should speak with him about his concerns and confusion.\n2\tTell Raphûz yes, you would follow your heart\030Tell Raphûz no, you would keep your promise\tRaphûz explained his concerns and asked you to give him your advice.\n3\tSpeak with Raphûz at his home in Jirush\tRaphûz wants to explain his decision. Speak with him at his home in Jirush.\n",
[313]="70016750\n1\tFill the water-skin with fresh water\030Find fresh water\tFresh water may be obtained in the small cave within the Shadowed Refuge. The Globsnaga Orcs' stagnant spring may be found at Dalgum-ru, south of the Shadowed Refuge. Tyki wants you to add clean water to the Globsnaga Orcs' foetid water in an effort to cure them of their fungal infection.\n2\tEmpty the water-skin into the Globsnaga Orcs' water\030Find the Globsnaga Orcs' water supply\tThe Globsnaga Orcs' stagnant spring is at Dalgum-ru, south of the Shadowed Refuge. Bring the water-skin of fresh water to the Orcs' water supply.\n3\tSpeak to Tyki at the Shadowed Refuge\tTyki is at the Shadowed Refuge, north of Dalgum-ru. You should return to Tyki and report back with the results of his freshwater cure.\n",
[314]="700303EB\n1\tSee what the Huorn wants\030Use the whistle to summon your new friend if you become separated\tThe Huorn is near the Orc-camp on the north-east edge of Fangorn's eaves.\n2\tComplete Orcs in Fangorn II\030Complete No Rest for Enemies\030Complete Mourning Felled Friends\tThis admiring Huorn wishes to help you deal with the dense population of Orcs in the White Hand encampment. You should complete a number of tasks in the encampment, using the whistle to call your tree-friend for help if you become separated.\n3\tTalk to the Huorn to dismiss him\tThe Huorn follows you as you venture throughout the White Hand encampment. You can use your whistle to summon it if you become separated. You should speak with the Huorn.\n4\tTalk to the old man who has been watching you\tA strange old man in rags hails you from north of the White Hand encampment. You should speak with this stranger....\n",
[315]="700097D9\n1\tTalk to Robin Dunkley\tRobin Dunkley lives in Ost Forod, north-east of Tinnudir in Tyrn Fornech, in Evendim. Calenglad has decided to meet with Gwindeth about acquiring the Silithar and has asked you to aid Robin Dunkley while he makes the journey.\n",
[316]="700323ED\n1\tSpeak with the trader at the Vault\030Speak with the trader at the Auction Hall\030Speak with the trader at the Crafting Hall\tThe friendly traders can be found outside of the Vault, Auction Hall, and Crafting Hall in Harwick. You should speak with each of the friendly traders and acquaint yourself with the town services of Harwick. Be wary of the guards!\n2\tCompleted\tYou have found the major town services of Harwick, and found friends amongst the sea of distrustful people loyal to Harding. You are not alone in these fair hard lands after all!\n",
[317]="7005718B\n1\tExplore Grazadh-gropor for signs of little-folk\tGrazadh-gropor can be found in the south-east part of Misthallow. You should search Grazadh-gropor for signs of little-folk.\n2\tTalk to Léothred at Thokvist\tLéothred can be found at Thokvist. You should talk to Léothred.\n3\tHead for the Cabed Rhimdath in Misthallow\tThe Cabed Rhimdath can be found west of Thokvist in Misthallow. You should head for the Cabed Rhimdath.\n4\tExplore the Cabed Rhimdath\tThe Cabed Rhimdath can be found in the south-west of Misthallow. You should explore the Cabed Rhimdath.\n5\tTalk to Fanglind in the Cabed Rhimdath\tThe Cabed Rhimdath can be found in the south-west of Misthallow. You should talk to Fanglind in the Cabed Rhimdath.\n6\tContinue exploring the Cabed Rhimdath\tThe Cabed Rhimdath can be found in the south-west of Misthallow. You should explore the Cabed Rhimdath.\n7\tTalk to Fanglind in the Cabed Rhimdath\tThe Cabed Rhimdath can be found in the south-west of Misthallow. You should talk to Fanglind in the Cabed Rhimdath.\n8\tExplore further into the Cabed Rhimdath\tThe Cabed Rhimdath can be found in the south-west of Misthallow. You should explore the Cabed Rhimdath.\n9\tTalk to Fanglind in the Cabed Rhimdath\tThe Cabed Rhimdath can be found in the south-west of Misthallow. You should talk to Fanglind in the Cabed Rhimdath.\n10\tTravel to the end of the Cabed Rhimdath\tThe Cabed Rhimdath can be found in the south-west of Misthallow. You should travel to the end of the Cabed Rhimdath.\n11\tTalk to Fanglind at Lyndelby\tFanglind is just outside Lyndelby in Misthallow. You should talk to Fanglind.\n12\tLearn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tLyndelby can be found in Misthallow. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n13\tContinue learning the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred\tLyndelby can be found in Misthallow. You should learn the history of the Rohirrim with Léothred.\n14\tTalk to Léothred at Lyndelby\tLéothred can be found in Lyndelby. You should talk to Léothred.\n15\tTalk to Léothred at Thokvist\tLéothred can be found at Thokvist. You should talk to Léothred.\n",
[318]="7000D127\n1\tTalk to Radagast the Brown\tRadagast the Brown can be found within his tower at the Eglain camp in Agamaur. You have been instructed to find Radagast the Brown and learn from him the art of speaking to the creatures of nature.\n",
[319]="7003567B\n1\tCall Mossbeard to your side\tMossbeard is standing at your side, or can be called with your whistle. Mossbeard has requested your aid in expediting his journey through Balewood. If you aid in completing his tasks, he will be able to return to Barallas and the other Ents more swiftly.\n2\tAid Mossbeard with Life in Darkness\030Aid Mossbeard with Cruel Blades\tMossbeard is at your side. Mossbeard has requested your aid in exploring the Balewood before returning to Barallas.\n3\tAid Mossbeard with Old Roots\tMossbeard is at your side. Mossbeard has communed with the trees of Balewood, and seeks to discover if they have spoken true. You should speak to him and learn what is to be done.\n4\tAid Mossbeard with Shattered Roots\tMossbeard is at your side. Mossbeard has communed with the trees and now wishes to tell you of the forest's past before relating the remainder of the story to his fellows.\n5\tReturn to Stonecliff with Mossbeard\tStonecliff is in northern Balewood. You have learned much of these woods in your time with Mossbeard. You should now return to Barallas and the others at Stonecliff.\n6\tTalk to Mossbeard\tMossbeard is at your side. You have returned to Stonecliff and should now speak to Mossbeard before he tells the rest of his tale to the Ents.\n7\tTalk to Barallas\tBarallas can be found at Stonecliff in northern Balewood. You have aided Mossbeard with all of his tasks. You should now return to Barallas at Stonecliff.\n",
[320]="700097DA\n1\tComplete Quest: The Corrupted Statue\030Complete Quest: The Lost Statue\tTwo statues of Elendil once stood on the south-east and south-west shores of Tyl Ruinen, but one statue has been corrupted by salamanders and the other statue is missing, perhaps recovered by the treasure-hunters of Ost Forod. The Eavespires are far to the north and east of Rushingdale. Gwindeth wants you to restore two statues of Elendil on Tyl Ruinen. Some Elves at the Eavespires may be able to prepare a cleansing draught for the corrupted statue. Gwindeth does not know where the missing statue may have ended up or in what condition it may be.\n2\tThe Blue Lady is in Gwindethrond, behind the waterfall at Rushingdale in western Emyn Uial, south-west of Tyl Ruinen. You have restored the two statues of Elendil on Tyl Ruinen, as Gwindeth requested, and should return to her with the news.\t\n",
})
